From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: acqxi <kacqxi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 07:46:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] Stats for nerds: thread and per-model turn performance

- The turn performance grid (the composer's last-turn popover and Thread
  details) gets a compact scope switch beside its title: Last turn, This
  thread (every finished main-agent turn, across provider sessions), and
  one entry per model once the thread has used two. The choice is kept
  per place in statsForNerdsPerformanceScopes ("last", "thread" or
  "model:<id>"); a model the thread never ran falls back to the last turn.
- Aggregates: TTFT and TTFA are medians with p90 in the tooltip; average
  tok/s is total generation tokens over total generation time of turns
  with at least 1 s of generation, estimated once any count was; peak is
  the highest turn peak; tokens, tool time and turn time are sums, partial
  when some turns did not report; cache hit is cached over input of the
  turns reporting both. Context and live speed are left out. The header
  shows the turn count, and the provider and model when one ran them all.
- A dense "micro" Toggle size for chips beside a popover title.
